### 4.3 Official STAR simulated MC sample

The STAR simulated MC samples of (1) \(\mu^{+}\) and \(\mu^{-}\) from \(J/\psi\) parents and (2) hadrons (\(\pi^{+}\), \(K^{+}\), proton, and their antiparticles) are used to calculate the detector efficiencies and acceptances. These particles, after generating by the single particle generator, are passed through full GEANT 3 [28] simulation of the STAR detector to obtain amounts of simulated signals. In order to mimic the reality, these signals are embedded into real events to have reasonable background distributions, and then they are reconstructed as simulated tracks by the same processes as we use for real data.

