#### MTD matching efficiency

The MTD matching efficiency is the probability of a reconstructed muon track that can be projected to an MTD module and matched to a hit on MTD. The difinition can be written as Eq. 5.7:

\[\varepsilon_{MTD}^{matching}=\frac{Number\ of\ muon\ track\ matched\ to\ MTD\ hit}{Number\ of\ muon\ track\ that\ can\ project\ to\ MTD\ module}. \tag{5.7}\]

This is an efficiency as a function of \(p_{T}^{\mu}\) with a plateau of 63% as shown in Fig. 5.6 which is evaluated by the official STAR simulated MC sample.

