#### Closure test of efficiency and acceptance

The closure test is used to ensure our efficiencies and acceptances are calculated correctly, and the MTD matching efficiency, \(J/\psi\) kinematic acceptance, and MTD geomatry acceptance are checked. In this closure test, the corrected distributions are obtained by using aforementioned efficiencies to correct the reconstructed samples (\(N_{Reco.}^{Corr.}\)), and then compared to the truth distributions (\(N_{Truth}\)). The result of closure test of MTD matching efficiency, \(J/\psi\) kinematic acceptance and MTD geometry acceptance are shown in Fig 5.42, Fig 5.43, and Fig 5.44, respectively. The ratios (\(\frac{N_{Reco.}^{Corr.}}{N_{Truth}}\)) are fitted by a constant function, and the results show that the closure tests are passed, i.e. the ratios are close to one.

